# iOS via Codemagic (from Windows)

Dev machine is Windows. There is **no** local Xcode. Never ask to open `.xcodeproj` / `.xcworkspace` by hand.

## Change iOS only through scripts / plists

| Goal | Where |
|------|--------|
| Brand / bundle / app group | `ios/scripts/apply_ios_brand.rb` + `BRAND=kpax\|xplm` |
| PacketTunnel target, Libbox link/embed | `ios/scripts/setup_packet_tunnel.rb` |
| Libbox binary | `ios/scripts/build_libbox.sh` (Codemagic step) |
| IPA contract | `ios/scripts/validate_ipa.py` |
| Pipeline | `codemagic.yaml` workflows `ios-testflight` / `ios-testflight-xplm` |

After changing tunnel/signing/embed logic: update `setup_packet_tunnel.rb` and the offline tests under `ios/scripts/test_*.py`. Bump `pubspec.yaml` build (`x.y.z+N`).

## Hard App Store / NE rules (learned)

- **Never** put `Frameworks/` inside `PacketTunnel.appex` (ASC **90205/90206**). Link Libbox in the extension; **embed** only in `Runner.app/Frameworks` and load via `@executable_path/../../Frameworks`.
- Normalize Libbox via `ios/scripts/normalize_libbox_framework.sh` (shallow slice, dylib, root + `Resources/Info.plist`). Refuse stubs / non-dylib (ASC **90171**).
- Do not re-sign with `--preserve-metadata` on an unsigned copy.
- Keep PacketTunnel / Runner versions from Flutter xcconfig (`FLUTTER_BUILD_*`).
- Signing on CI: `app-store-connect fetch-signing-files` + `xcode-project use-profiles` (integration `kpax`). No local certs.

## codemagic.yaml

- Validate YAML indentation when editing.
- Keep `validate_ipa.py --brand …` after `flutter build ipa`.
- Brands: K-Pax `space.kpax.app` / X-Plm `online.xplm.app` (+ `.extension`, `group.*`).
- Prefer targeted local checks over burning CI minutes (see `pre-push-guard`).
